<title>USA: ADR REPORT - Abacan moves higher.</title>
<headline>ADR REPORT - Abacan moves higher.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian oil company Abacan Resource Corp moved higher Tuesday to stand out among American depositary receipts ADRs and foreign shares.</p>
<p>Shares in the Calgary-based company were up 3/8 to 2-5/8. Volume was very heavy at 5.8 million shares in late morning, and Abacan was the most-active foreign share.</p>
<p>Calgary-based Abacan fell more than 50 percent Monday  after it said its 1997 cash flow would be much lower than analysts' predictions.  </p>
<p>Chief Executive Wade Cherwayko said Monday investors had overreacted to the news and the company's operations remained intact.</p>
<p>Among other active foreign shares, Canada's Philip Services Corp fell 1/4 to 14-1/4 and Australia's News Corp preferred</p>
<p>Telefonica del Peru fell 7/8 to 25-3/8 after Merrill Lynch cut its near-term rating on the stock to accumulate from buy. The firm maintained its rating of long-term buy on the ADRs.  </p>
<p>ADRs allow U.S. trade of foreign shares.</p>
<p>((-- Wall Street desk (212) 859-1730))</p>
</text>
